      "writtenOn": "2018-03-23T02:17:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "System apps don\u0027t automatically get restricted networks. They have to clear the NOT_RESTRICTED bit from the capabilities.\n\nAn app that wanted a network with Internet access would never have needed to do this, because a network with Internet access has until now been guaranteed to be unrestricted. So I don\u0027t think there is any existing code that could now start getting an network with INTERNET and OEM_PAID by mistake.\n\nCode in the system that called clearCapabilities() could be getting OEM_PAID INTERNET networks regardless of what we do here.\n\nISTM that mean we don\u0027t need to add OEM_PAID to the unwanted set by default, because no app will be getting this without expecting it. Are there cases I\u0027m missing?\n\n(Note: I\u0027m not strongly opposed to doing this, but this code does have a lot of callers, and this sort of change hasn\u0027t been made before, so if we can live without it, that would be preferable.)",
      "parentUuid": "dbe2ce86_9e44ba9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 59
      },
